<html>
<head>
	<title></title>
</head>
<body style="height: auto; min-height: auto;">Ref No: {{{Case.Case_Number__c}}}<br />
<br />
Hi {{{Case.First_Name__c}}},<br />
<br />
Thank you for contacting us about your experience in {{{Case.Departure_City__c}}} on {{{Case.Email_Departure_Date_Time__c}}}.<br />
<br />
<em><strong>-If overbooking use:-</strong></em><br />
<br />
I'm sorry to hear to that your cabin was changed on our QF{{{Case.Flight_Number__c}}} flight. I understand how disappointing this must have been and would like to apologise for the inconvenience caused.<br />
<br />
<em><strong>-If aircraft downgrade use:-</strong></em><br />
<br />
I was sorry to learn that your cabin was changed on our QF{{{Case.Flight_Number__c}}} flight. I understand how disappointing this must have been.<br />
<br />
The original aircraft you were on was impacted due to a mechanical problem.<br />
<br />
Configurations can vary from service to service and the only alternative aircraft available had less seats in the -First/Business/Premium Economy- Class cabin.<br />
<br />
<em><strong>-If rebooked due delayed inbound use:-</strong></em><br />
<br />
I was sorry to learn about your delayed flight in to {{{Case.Arrival_City__c}}}, and the impact this had on your connecting flight to -final destination-. To get you on your way the only alternative was in -DOWNGRADED- Class. I understand how disappointing this must have been.<br />
<br />
You’ll need to speak to -your travel agent/AIRLINE- regarding your fare - as they issued your tickets they will need to calculate if there is any refundable fare differential between the original ticket purchased and the class flown.<br />
<br />
<em><strong>-If downgrade comp provided add:-</strong></em><br />
<br />
I believe our airport staff have already arranged ${{{Case.Recovery_Value__c}}} downgrade compensation for you as a token of our appreciation.<br />
<br />
<em><strong>-If EMD issued by airport needs to be refunded:-&nbsp;</strong></em><br />
<br />
I can see that our airport staff have arranged a ${{{Case.Recovery_Value__c}}} voucher as downgrade compensation. We’d be happy to process the payment for you and I‘ve attached a form for you to provide your bank account details.<br />
<br />
When returning the completed form, please reply to this email to make sure your information is attached to your file and processed as soon as possible.&nbsp;<br />
<br />
<em><strong>-If downgrade comp not provided and through-fare add:-</strong></em><br />
<br />
<em><strong>-If a Frequent Flyer:-</strong></em><br />
<br />
As a token of our appreciation, I’ve credited {{{Case.Recovery_Quantity__c}}} Qantas Points to your Frequent Flyer account.<br />
<br />
<br />
<em><strong>-If not a Frequent Flyer:-</strong></em><br />
<br />
As a token of our appreciation, I’d like to arrange a credit of {{{Case.Recovery_Quantity__c}}} Qantas Points to you.<br />
<br />
Please can you let me know your Frequent Flyer number by replying to this email so I can credit points to your account. If you’re not already a member you can use this&nbsp;<a href="https://www.qantas.com/en-au/frequent-flyer/join/code/familyfree">link</a>&nbsp;to join free of charge.<br />
<br />
<br />
<strong>We value your opinion</strong><br />
<br />
Customer feedback plays an important role in our continuous improvement process so that we can provide you with exceptional service from start to finish.<br />
<br />
I wanted to assure you that I’ve passed your comments on to the relevant team. Thank you again for telling us about your experience.</body>
</html>